We want to consider whether this correlation is significant for $\alpha = 0.05$. If the data is not normally distributed we use the Spearman correlation, which is computed using the rank of the data, $rank_x, rank_y$, and defined by $r_s = s_{rank_x rank_y}/(s_{rank_x}s_{rank_y})$ for the general case when there may be ties.

